.TH SWAPOFF 8 "August 2026" ReBSD
.SH NAME
swapoff \- disable a swap device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swapoff
.I special
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B swapoff
stops new allocations on the named swap device, pages in every anonymous
page still backed by it, and then closes the device.  Other configured swap
devices remain active.  The operation fails without changing the active
device set if insufficient physical memory prevents the remaining pages from
being made resident.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
swapoff /dev/wd0b
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swapon (8),
.BR free (1),
.BR pstat (8)
